!
! This test shows the use of the atomic shift projector
! We consider the carbon monoxide molecule.
! From a straightforward Hartree-Fock calculation and Mulliken population analysis
!
!  * Electronic eigenvalue no.   1: -20.684805978275       (Occupation : f = 1.0000)  m_j=  1/2
!  ============================================================================================
!  
!  * Gross populations greater than 0.01000
!  
!  Gross     Total   |    L A1 O  s   
!  --------------------------------------
!   alpha    0.9995  |      0.9992
!   beta     0.0005  |      0.0000
!  
!  * Electronic eigenvalue no.   2: -11.369805625232       (Occupation : f = 1.0000)  m_j=  1/2
!  ============================================================================================
!  
!  * Gross populations greater than 0.01000
!  
!  Gross     Total   |    L A1 C  s   
!  --------------------------------------
!   alpha    0.9997  |      0.9990
!   beta     0.0003  |      0.0000
!
! we find that the two lowest molecular orbitals are correspond to O1s and C1s with an orbital energy gap of 9.315 Hartrees.
!
! We introduce a shift operator build from a pre-calculated C1s orbital and a downward energy shift corresponding to this gap.
! We now find:
!
!  * Electronic eigenvalue no.   1: -20.687541430101       (Occupation : f = 1.0000)  m_j=  1/2
!  ============================================================================================
!  
!  * Gross populations greater than 0.01000
!  
!  Gross     Total   |    L A1 C  s      L A1 O  s   
!  -----------------------------------------------------
!   alpha    0.9996  |      0.4790         0.5203
!   beta     0.0004  |      0.0000         0.0000
!  
!  * Electronic eigenvalue no.   2: -20.681935949730       (Occupation : f = 1.0000)  m_j=  1/2
!  ============================================================================================
!  
!  * Gross populations greater than 0.01000
!  
!  Gross     Total   |    L A1 C  s      L A1 O  s   
!  -----------------------------------------------------
!   alpha    0.9996  |      0.5202         0.4790
!   beta     0.0004  |      0.0000         0.0000
!  
! showing that we brought the O1s and C1s orbitals. We now see a "bonding" and "anti-bonding" MO. This is clearly
! artificial. We have seen degeneracy-driven orbital mixing, but it does not create bonds.
!

